        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Assigns the new values in \ref vals to &apos;part&apos;, by forwarding to
:cpp:func:`IfContentPart::replaceVals` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

Every conditional spec&apos;s \ref ModTypePredicate is first bound against &apos;modType&apos; to
produce the plain single-argument :cpp:type:`IfContentPart::Predicate`
:cpp:func:`IfContentPart::replaceVals` expects -- which is why this class keeps its
own spec type instead of reusing :cpp:type:`IfContentPart::ReplaceSpec` directly
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>part</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The part of the <computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_if_template" kindref="compound">IfTemplate</ref></computeroutput> being edited, modified in place </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>sectionName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the <computeroutput>section</computeroutput>_ being edited. Unused by this edit </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modType</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of mod to fix, or <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput>. Unused by this edit. <bold>Default</bold>: <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the mod to fix to. Unused by this edit. <bold>Default</bold>: <computeroutput>""</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>partRanges</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The valid order indices to process for &apos;part&apos;, or <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput> for all of them. <bold>Default</bold>: <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The same part that was passed in, after editing </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
